?w=1200&h=630&q=50&fit=fill"}},"body":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"html":"<h2>Commit to Deploy Time</h2>\n<p>The time to take the code from commit to a deployment environment.\n<strong>Measurement</strong>: Record the time elasted from code review to the code is merged.</p>\n<h2>Build Time</h2>\n<p>The time to build the changes, (runing unit test, integration test)\nA good example: 10 mins build time will cost $9 per engineer who gets paid $54 per hour, when they are waiting for build completion. Considering in a team of 5 engineers, and 2 of them neends to wait for the build 5 times day, it will cost $450 per week, and $21600 per year.\n<strong>Measurement</strong>: Time to setup, tear down testing environment and runing the test.</p>","timeToRead":1}},"tags":["engineering management"],"description":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"excerpt":"Some metrics to understand the engineering efficiency"}}},"previous":null,"next":{"slug":"clean-code","title":"Clean code"}},"pageContext":{"slug":"engineering-metrics","previousPostSlug":null,"nextPostSlug":"clean-code"}},
